# Target C-II — `g=0.0077` residual stability raises the full-core floor to `1.843577`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only downstream strengthening  
**Scope:** full-core Type-II branch  
**Dependencies:** corrected scope-safe `g=0.0077` phase-star capacity; `g=0.0076` residual-coupled scalar theorem; hostile-audited joint endpoint retention and complement-rhombus incidence  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The current residual-coupled theorem uses the matched atomic input

\[
C_{76}=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.0076,
\qquad
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},
\]

and proves

\[
\liminf {q-k\over D}\ge1.843555.
\]

The corrected three-branch phase-star capacity now gives the stronger safe input

\[
\boxed{C_{77}=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.0077.}
\tag{R77.1}
\]

The residual-stability and feasible-triangle arguments survive with the same convenient
constant `c=1.05`.  Substituting `C77` and certifying the new corner gives

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-k\over D}\ge1.843577.
}
\tag{R77.2}
\]

A non-load-bearing high-precision solve of the corner equation is

\[
t_*=1.8435775982814395\ldots .
\]

Only the rationally certified value `1.843577` is claimed.

---

## 1. Residual stability at `C77`

Write

\[
t={q-k\over D},\qquad
\kappa={k\over D},\qquad
\delta={d_{out}\over D},
\]

and

\[
U={9t\over2}-2\pi-2\delta-\kappa/2.
\tag{R77.3}
\]

Let `M` be the mass of a dominant exact projective `pi/3` orbit and put

\[
h:=U-C_{77},\qquad R:=U-M.
\]

The corrected `g=.0077` theorem proves that the full physical one-orbit capacity
`Psi(W)` is strictly below `Delta2` at `W=C77`.  On the only interval needed when
`M<C77`, namely the generic two-bin localization range below `C77`, the exact branch
derivatives give the uniform lower slope

\[
\boxed{
\Psi(C_{77})-\Psi(W)>0.596(C_{77}-W).
}
\tag{R77.4}
\]

The strong branch actually has derivative above `0.6058`; the fallback and high-center
branches are larger.  The rounded `0.596` is used only to keep the stability algebra
transparent.

As in the `g=.0076` theorem, the generic two-bin bound on the whole live range
`U<=2.013` gives

\[
R<0.112.
\tag{R77.5}
\]

The exact orbit decomposition gives

\[
\Delta_2\le\Psi(M)+{R^2\over4}.
\tag{R77.6}
\]

If `M>=C77`, then `R<=h`.  If `M<C77`, combine (R77.4)--(R77.6) and discard the
additional positive endpoint margin at `C77` to obtain

\[
0.596(C_{77}-M)<{R^2\over4}.
\]

Since `C77-M=R-h`,

\[
R-h<{R^2\over4(0.596)}.
\]

Using (R77.5),

\[
R
< {h\over1-0.112/[4(0.596)]}
<1.05h.
\]

Therefore throughout `C77<=U<=2.013`,

\[
\boxed{0\le U-M\le1.05(U-C_{77}).}
\tag{R77.7}
\]

This is the only new stability input required downstream.

---

## 2. The residual-coupled survivor system is unchanged

Put

\[
x={\kappa\over2},\qquad c=1.05.
\]

Equation (R77.3) becomes

\[
\boxed{
2\delta+x+h
=R_t:={9t\over2}-2\pi-C_{77}.
}
\tag{R77.8}
\]

Exactly as in the hostile-audited `g=.0076` scalar theorem, shared routewise retention
and (R77.7) give retained dominant outer-occurrence mass `z` and complement O--O pair
mass `p` satisfying

\[
z+p\ge\pi-{t\over2}-x-ch-o(1).
\tag{R77.9}
\]

The complement-rhombus incidence budget is at most the square of the same residual:

\[
p(1-\delta)-{e_c\over2}
\le {c^2h^2\over2}+o(1).
\tag{R77.10}
\]

If

\[
F(z)=z-6\sin(z/6),
\]

then the retained dominant occurrences consume at least `F(z)D-o(D)` of the exact outer
directional energy, and the selected dominant and complement supports are disjoint.  Thus

\[
e_c\le\delta-F(z)+o(1),
\tag{R77.11}
\]

and every survivor satisfies `F(z)<=delta+o(1)`.

Eliminating `p` gives the same survivor-capacity function as before:

\[
Q(t,h,x)=
F^{-1}(\delta)
+{c^2h^2\over2(1-\delta)}
-\left(\pi-{t\over2}-x-ch\right),
\tag{R77.12}
\]

with

\[
\delta={R_t-x-h\over2}.
\]

Survival requires

\[
Q(t,h,x)\ge0.
\tag{R77.13}
\]

---

## 3. The full feasible triangle again collapses to one corner

For `t<=1.843577`, the exact verifier proves

\[
U<2.013,\qquad
\delta<0.051,\qquad
h<0.101.
\tag{R77.14}
\]

On `0<=z<=pi`,

\[
F'(z)=1-\cos(z/6)<0.134.
\]

Therefore the derivatives used by the `g=.0076` proof remain valid without any change
of sign.  In particular,

\[
Q_x
=-{1\over2F'(F^{-1}\delta)}
-{c^2h^2\over4(1-\delta)^2}+1
<-2.7,
\tag{R77.15}
\]

and

\[
Q_h
=-{1\over2F'(F^{-1}\delta)}
+c+{c^2h\over1-\delta}
-{c^2h^2\over4(1-\delta)^2}
<-2.5.
\tag{R77.16}
\]

Also `Q_t>0`.  Hence, for fixed `t`, survivor capacity is maximized at

\[
\boxed{x=0,\qquad h=0.}
\tag{R77.17}
\]

Thus no interior topology or residual-orbit allocation is weaker than the matched
corner.

---

## 4. Exact corner certificate

At the corner,

\[
\delta_0(t)
={1\over2}\left({9t\over2}-2\pi-C_{77}\right),
\]

and survival requires

\[
\boxed{
\delta_0(t)
\ge F\left(\pi-{t\over2}\right).
}
\tag{R77.18}
\]

The exact verifier

`research/verify_target_c_g0077_residual_stability_floor_1843577.py`

uses only `Fraction` arithmetic, Machin enclosures for `pi`, integer-square-root bounds,
and alternating Taylor bounds for `sin`.  It proves

\[
F\left(\pi-{1.843577\over2}\right)-\delta_0(1.843577)
>1.36\times10^{-6},
\tag{R77.19}
\]

so `t=1.843577` is impossible.  The same certificate proves that the corresponding
margin at `1.843578` is negative, consistent with the numerical root
`1.84357759828...`.

Since `Q_t>0`, all smaller `t` are excluded as well.  This proves (R77.2).

---

## 5. Frontier effect

The numerical gain is modest,

\[
1.843577-1.843555=2.2\times10^{-5},
\]

but the proof is clean: the stronger atomic theorem propagates through the complete
correlated feasible triangle without introducing a new relaxation.

At the weakest corner,

\[
U=C_{77},\qquad U-M=0,\qquad\kappa=0,
\]

so all exact atomic mass is forced into one exact three-phase orbit and the independent
complement-rhombus budget vanishes.  The new small-leaf O--O rectangle and `>0.73D`
center-fan theorems should therefore be attacked directly rather than further optimizing
residual mass.

No C-II or Level-I closure is claimed.
